    "With a budget for the top 20% (282 customers), 'Churn risk' ranking gives the highest profit: $37,264 (ROI 264%) vs $28,476 for uplift and $2,383 for random targeting.",
    "Most profitable overall: 'Churn risk' contacting the top 40% (profit $42,459). Contacting more than that REDUCES profit: extra offers go to customers who would stay anyway or who react badly.",
    "Uplift ranking avoids 'lost causes' (high-risk customers the offer cannot save), but in this simulation churn risk already captures most of who responds, so it wins on profit.",
    "Recommendation: target the highest churn-risk customers first, skip customers the uplift model flags as negative (likely to react badly), and run a real A/B test before trusting uplift scores, because the uplift effects here are simulated."
